    historyContent: {
      origins: 'Turbo Hearts was introduced at the University of Pennsylvania in the 1980s by Richard Garfield (later creator of Magic: The Gathering). It is an American variant of the Hearts family and an American version of the Chinese game Gong Zhu (Catch the Pig). The parent game Hearts emerged in the United States in the 1880s and descends from earlier trick-avoidance games such as Reversis.',
